            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0196" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.34537/38.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-12-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1910</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 502.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: While referring to previous correspondence,
                    and in order that there may be no misunderstanding, I have the honor to inform
                    you that I have not taken up officially in any way with the Cuban Government the
                    question of the enlargement of our naval station at Guantánamo, and the possible
                    renunciation of the Bahía Honda lease. Clippings from La Lucha, which have been
                    sent the Department in the usual way, would appear to indicate that I have
                    already begun, negotiations in the premises.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
